    "['local-user [parameter1] password irreversible-cipher [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user nms2-admin authentication encrypted-password \"$9$n}=%C*UimYlx9-:$>T=*_y4PX*e~u6I_Aa9s=I1\"', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the specified HUAWEI command:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user nms2-admin authentication encrypted-password \"$9$n}=%C*UimYlx9-:$>T=*_y4PX*e~u6I_Aa9s=I1\"\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"$9$\" prefix to denote an encrypted/irreversible password format (similar to HUAWEI\\'s irreversible-cipher)\\n2. I\\'ve removed the HUAWEI-specific %#%# delimiters as Juniper has its own password formatting\\n3. The actual encrypted password string remains the same as it\\'s already in an irreversible format\\n4. This creates a local user with the same authentication credentials, though you would need additional Juniper commands to configure SNMP access rights equivalent to the HUAWEI configuration', 'trans_template': 'set system login user nms2-admin authentication encrypted-password \"$9$n}=%C*UimYlx9-:$>T=*_y4PX*e~u6I_Aa9s=I1\"'}]]": 1,
