    "['local-user [parameter1] user-group [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user nms2-admin class grp1', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here is the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI configuration `local-user nms2-admin user-group grp1`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user nms2-admin class grp1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `set system login user` defines a local user, similar to HUAWEI's `local-user`.\\n- The `class` parameter assigns the user to a group, which is equivalent to HUAWEI's `user-group` assignment.\\n- The group name `grp1` is preserved in the translation.\", 'trans_template': 'set system login user nms2-admin class grp1'}]]": 1,
    "['task-group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login class tg1 permissions configure', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration for the Huawei `task-group` command:\\n\\n##\\nset system login class tg1 permissions configure\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, login classes define permissions similar to Huawei's task groups. \\n- The `permissions configure` grants write permissions, equivalent to the `task snmp write` in the Huawei configuration.\\n- The class name `tg1` is preserved to match the original configuration.\\n\\nNote that Juniper handles SNMP permissions differently, and additional SNMP-specific configuration would be needed to fully replicate the Huawei setup, but this is the direct equivalent of the task-group definition.\", 'trans_template': 'set system login class tg1 permissions configure'}]]": 1,
    "['task [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login class grp1 permissions [ configure snmp ]', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'set system login class tg1 permissions configure'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent for the HUAWEI command `task snmp write`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login class grp1 permissions [ configure snmp ]\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, permissions are assigned through login classes (similar to HUAWEI's task-groups)\\n- The `configure` permission allows configuration changes\\n- The `snmp` permission specifically grants SNMP configuration access\\n- This creates equivalent SNMP write privileges as the HUAWEI command\", 'trans_template': 'set system login class grp1 permissions [ configure snmp ]'}]]": 1,
    "['user-group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set groups grp1', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset groups grp1\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact equivalent functionality may vary between Huawei and Juniper. In Juniper, `user-group` is typically mapped to `groups` for configuration grouping, but the specific task-group associations would need to be handled separately in Juniper's policy framework. The above provides the basic structural translation.\", 'trans_template': 'set groups grp1'}]]": 1,
    "['task-group [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login class tg1 permissions [ configure snmp ]', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'set groups grp1'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the HUAWEI `task-group` command:\\n\\n##\\nset system login class tg1 permissions [ configure snmp ]\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, permissions are managed through \"login classes\" instead of \"task groups\"\\n- The `configure` permission allows write access (equivalent to HUAWEI\\'s `write` permission)\\n- The `snmp` permission grants SNMP configuration access\\n- This creates a class named \"tg1\" with equivalent SNMP write privileges', 'trans_template': 'set system login class tg1 permissions [ configure snmp ]'}]]": 1,
    "['task [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login class grp1 permissions configure', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'set groups grp1', 'set system login class tg1 permissions [ configure snmp ]'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-association [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for `task snmp write`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login class grp1 permissions configure\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei, `task snmp write` is part of a task group that grants SNMP write permissions\\n- In Juniper, we create a login class with equivalent permissions using the `configure` permission level, which allows write access (similar to SNMP write capabilities)\\n- The class name `grp1` is maintained to match the original user-group association\", 'trans_template': 'set system login class grp1 permissions configure'}]]": 1,
